  "proof_supplied": [
    "Finite bumps construct smooth weights and a shrunk cover; uniform closeness needed only on explicitly compact overlap sets.",
    "Explicit quaternionic average S_i=\u03a3\u03c6_j h_ij^n h_ji stays nearI and nonzero. Quaternionic real matrix algebra gives S_i*S_i=lambda_i\u00b2I and detS_i=lambda_i\u00b2. Scalar normalization supplies actualSU2 maps.",
    "Exact identity S_i=h_ik^n S_k h_ki and unitary invariance oflambda give actual cocycle isomorphism pointwise.",
    "LocalW2,12/5 algebra via L\u221e andDL6 products, plus fully justified smooth normalization composition, give sigma_i^n\u2192I stronglyW2,12/5loc and uniformlycompact.",
    "Gauge-transferred connection forms use the fixed LIMIT cocycle exactly. Explicit derivative product estimates give b_i^n\u2212a_i^n\u21920 stronglyW1,2loc and preserve weakW1,2, strongLp<4, curvatureweakL2 and ASD convergence."
  ],
  "precise_scope": "Finite Euclidean ball cover of a compact set; continuousSU2 cocycles, strongW2,12/5loc and uniformcompact convergence; covershrinking explicit. Transferred forms need not remainCoulomb.",
